<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Ernest, Grand Duke of Saxe-Weimar-Eisenach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1876–1923</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Wilhelm Ernst</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Ernest was the last Grand Duke of Saxe-Weimar-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenach">Eisenach</a>, reigning from 1901 until the German Revolution. He was an unpopular, authoritarian ruler, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a>'s art school and the reformist designer Henry van de Velde flourished under his patronage. He abdicated on 9 November 1918, and in 1920 his former grand duchy became part of the new Land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-ernest-grand-duke-of-saxe-weimar-eisenach.jpg" alt="William Ernest, Grand Duke of Saxe-Weimar-Eisenach" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otto Hoffmann, Weimar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GrandDukeWILHELM.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
